          ],
          "content": "Q.3. If Floor A = − 12, Floor D = − 1 and Floor E = + 1 in the building shown on the right as a line, find the numbers of Floors B, C, F, G and H. Ans. B = -9 C = -6 $\\mathrm{F}=+2\\mathrm{~G}=+6\\mathrm{~H}=+11$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.156,
            0.688,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": "Q.4. Mark the following floors of the building shown on the right. a.-7 b. -4 c. +3 d. -10 Ans. a. P = -7 b. Q = - 4 c. R = +3 d. S = -10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.266,
            0.203,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "Page 248"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.292,
            0.635,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "Q. Evaluate 15 – 5, 100 – 10 and 74 – 34 from this perspective."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.322,
            0.582,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "15 -5 can be expressed as 5 + ? = 15 . So, ? = 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.341,
            0.62,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": "100 – 10 can be expressed as 10 + ? = 100. So, ? = 90"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.36,
            0.601,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "74 – 34 can be expressed as 34 + ? = 74. So, ? = 40"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.403,
            0.237,
            0.422
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 249"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.431,
            0.235,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": "Figure it out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.457,
            0.885,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "Q. Complete these expressions. You may think of them as finding the movement needed to reach the Target Floor from the Starting Floor. a. (+ 1) − (+ 4) = b. (0) − (+ 2) = c. (+ 4) − (+ 1) = d. (0) − (− 2) = e. (+ 4) − (−3) = f.(−4) − (−3) = g. (− 1) − (+ 2) = h. (− 2) − (− 2) 二i. (− 1) − (+1) = j. (+ 3) − (− 3) =."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.665,
            0.301,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "Ans. a. (-3) b. (-2) c. (+3) d. (+2) e. (+7) f. (-1) g. (-3) h. (0) i. (-2) j.(+6)"
